ar a path for eren to reach him  however before the two of them are able  to make contact the cart titan fakes her  own death which causes both zeke and the  igress to let their guard down in the  process nearly the entire group of  jaegerson or mario were ambushed with  flock being the sole survivor and at the  same time magath gets a clean shot that  tears through half of the beast titan  spine meanwhile arm and mikasa and the  other prisoners were freed from their  cells and allowed to fight directly  leading to several malian soldiers  getting blown up by thunderspears at  this stage the war was slowly turning  into more of an even contest and in a  weird way things got better for the  scouts once zeke turned half their army  into pure titans although it is sad that  pixes and the rest of them were turned  into monsters it's undeniable that them  being pure titans made it way easier to  fight back against the invasion across  the ganchiner every last marlin soldier  would either be eaten alive by these  things or dealt with by the scouts with  mcgath being one of the only regular  humans who was able to escape from the  front lines before we skip too far ahead  though we should probably mention that  when zeke did his scream the electricity  from falco's titan fried colt to a crisp  this death was especially tragic for two  reasons number one because cult was  betrayed by a person who was meant to be  his mentor and number two the warrior  candidate sacrificed himself so that he  could be with his younger brother as he  transformed following the transformation  pure titan falco then makes arguably the  most significant kill from part 2 as he  inherits the draw titan by chewing  galliard to pieces this was only the  second time this season that a titan  shifter had been killed by someone but  in porko's case he willingly allowed it  to happen since he didn't have enough  stamina to heal his existing injuries  now after this moment there weren't any  more fatalities for episode 19 besides  some random background shoulders getting  eaten but still it'd be weird to move on  without highlighting eren's near-death  experience in this iconic scene the yaga  bros were just meters away from making  contact but gabby who quite literally  never misses a shot manages to hit his  neck with an anti-titan rifle this sends  aaron's head spinning through the air  and it's undeniable that if he had  landed anywhere else other than zeke's  hand then that would have been the end  of attack on titan fortunately for us  the story continues with both brothers  ending up in the past dimension and in  episode 20 the kill count gets added to  when aaron convinces grisha to squash  the royal family in total this meant the  death of six people including five of  historia's siblings but as we know rod  rice was able to escape so that one day  he could be blown up by the scouts  instead  speaking of the royal family episode 21  takes us 2 thousand years into the past  where we get to witness the origin of  the royal bloodline during this  backstory we see that ymir lived in a  tiny village that couldn't have had a  population of more than 300 and most of  them were wiped out when the eldians  chose to invade some time after this  king fritz used emir's founding titan to  destroy a small army of malian soldiers  and years later after she gave birth to  mario she personally crushes an even  larger group of soldiers with their bare  hands these defeats caused the marlins  to feel a ton of resentment towards the  alien empire and when they arrived to  surrender to fitz one of the soldiers  had pre-planted a spear on the ground  which they then used to throw at the  king unfortunately fritz wasn't the one  to take the head as you may have jumped  in the way to protect him and  surprisingly this attack did kill her  mainly because she didn't have the will  to live the malian assassin who threw  the spear was then sliced to pieces by  nearby aldean guards and in the manga  version of this scene it's shown that  the guards also killed the soldiers who  were kneeling next to him when it comes  to king fritz himself he ended up on his  deathbed presumably due to natural  causes and we know it couldn't have been  that long after the assassination  attempt since his daughters hadn't  really grown much between the two  incidents switching over to aaron  activating the rumbling in the present  day this instantly caused the deaths of  thousands of eldians across parodies  island the main reason for these deaths  was that aaron crumbled all three walls  without giving people time to prepare  which meant that anyone who lived next  to them had a high chance of being  crushed when we take a quick look at  this map shigachina was the only town  near the walls that had already been  evacuated whereas the remaining  districts like trost and stowers had  extensive casualties and we saw this in  episode 22. a safe estimate would be  that around 400 people per district were  flattened which is easily more than 4  000 alden deaths caused by aaron overall  now back in trigancina zeke's pure  titans had finished eating all the  malian soldiers and began turning their  attention to the surviving scouts during  the chaos a handful of scouts were  explicitly shown to either be smushed or  eaten alive and you'd have to imagine  there were an extra 20 to 30 soldiers we  didn't see who probably got the same  treatment eventually though jean was  able to lead the scouts to kill every  pure titan in the district with the two  most significant deaths being pixies and  nile in nars case gabby killed him using  the same rifle she used to decapitate  eren and in pixis's case a very sorry  armin had to blow him up using a  thunderspear following this the next  death came from one of the anti-marlin  volunteers who was murdered by flock to  show the other volunteers what could  happen flock's main goal at this point  was to eliminate people on the island  who didn't support the alien empire and  of course the volunteers weren't exactly  keen on helping given that aaron was  about to destroy their homelands the  volunteer who flock executed was the  most vocal out of the group and his  death did have some kind of impact as it  made jon question whether he was on the  right side  in episode 24 hanji and levi were being  hunted down by the yagaris and while  hiding in the forest the commander  tearfully shoots two soldiers that were  chasing after them later on it's heavily  implied that these two weren't the only  ones they had to kill and when we  flashed back to when hanji first escaped  we do see there was a third person they  must have killed off screen around  halfway through the episode things then  switch over to a random hospital where  mikasa pays a visit to louise while it's  true that louise doesn't die in this  exact moment she reveals that she has  shrapnel inside her system which is  basically a death sentence for anyone  who doesn't have one of these things  what makes her death especially tragic  is that it could have been prevented  because the only reason she got hurt was  that she spent too much time staring at  mikasa in the middle of a war zone it  was this distraction that led to her  getting caught up in the explosion but  if she'd been paying attention then  she'd very likely still be alive  anyway moving on episode 25 was the  first and only episode from part 2 not  to have a single person die primarily  because most of the runtime was the  alliance having various debates and  beating each other up by the end though  they did eventually make it to the  harbour which is when the kill count  dramatically began to increase for a  start hanji mentions how the yeagers  have killed four people already  referring to the azmobito engineers who  were likely shot by flock on top of that  based on the speed of the titans the  commander worked out that several malian  cities on the coast had already been  trampled although we don't have an exact  figure it's safe to assume that a few  coastal cities is equivalent to at least  a couple million people and remember  this doesn't even factor in liberia it  wasn't until much later on that hanji  realized liberia would also be crushed  as well which by my estimation adds  another 500 000 civilians to the kill  count it's important to remember that  liberio is more than just the people  inside the internment zone as it also  has large sections where malians live  and work not to mention tens of  thousands of soldiers who do special  training up in the mountains  now when it comes to the alliance  despite armin trying to take the  peaceful path he couldn't prevent things  turning into an all-out war between the  scouts and the agres in the beginning of  this war hanji and magath killed three  jaegers inside one of the main buildings  while annie and reina pummeled nearly 10  soldiers with their bare hands meanwhile  next to the flying boat connie made the  gut-wrenching choice to execute daz and  samuel who are two friends that he's  known ever since their time in the  cadets ultimately connie had to make  this decision in order for the alliance  to have a chance of stopping eren and in  the background the warriors continued to  get a nice amount of kills with mikasa  joining the action as well when the  fighting first began she did actually  hurt to jaegerus already although it  wasn't clear if she killed them but  assuming that she knocked them  unconscious the two soldiers would have  been blown to pieces when other jaegers  fired into the room anyhow magath and  hanji added to their kill streets while  the azmobito tried to escape however a  train full of jaeger's reinforcements  was heading towards the harbour in total  there were 9 visible carriages with  roughly 15 soldiers each which we can  round up to 150 overall if those  reinforcements had made it to where they  needed to be then the alliance for sure  would have been overwhelmed by the  numbers hence why instructor chad has  stepped in to blow it up by doing what  he did he gave the alliance their final  chance of surviving and in the next  scene when annie and reina were about to  be killed connie saves them by  single-handedly wiping out five jaegris  mikasa follows that up by slicing four  of them herself and in total i guess  that around 80 plus jagras were taken  out by this small group of fighters on  one hand you could argue that it's  realistic given that these are the  island's best soldiers besides captain  levi but personally i did think it was  kind of weird that they were able to get  through this without anyone being shot  or taking serious damage to their human  bodies regardless once the battle was  over general mcgath stayed behind to  make sure the yaegris wouldn't be able  to chase after the alliance and in the  process he and charles had a bit of a  team up on his introduction the  instructor personally killed a couple of  soldiers that were chasing after mcgath  and then the two men boarded one of the  nearby cruisers their plan was to  destroy this thing so that the jaegers  couldn't use it but to do this mission  it involved them getting blown up as  well technically speaking shardis had  the option to leave the ship and survive  if he wanted to but he already made it  clear that he didn't see a future on the  island while people like flock were in  charge as a consequence both of them  died when magath ignites the gunpowder  and it evaporates everybody on board  including the enemy soldiers  finally moving on to the grand finale of  part 2 all the casualties in this one  came in the last few minutes of the  episode on the malian coast the global  military alliance had assembled the  strongest cannons humanity had to offer  and overall there were over 90  battleships confirmed by this screenshot  here if the average crew size is 120 men  per ship then that's easily 10 000 plus  soldiers not to mention the thousands  more who are on dry land the cannons  then begin firing towards the rumbling  and to be fair they do some damage to  the colossal titans in the front but it  didn't take a second for the hordes of  titans behind them to overtake these  monsters then swim underneath the ships  causing most of them to be flung into  the air by the hot steam but some  unlucky soldiers on board did also get  burned up before that happened gradually  all 10 000 men would be wiped out when  their ships exploded on impact and on  the shore scores of malian troops begin  to abandon their stations as error  marches forward we then get a bird's eye  view of the rumbling destroying  everything although the kill count  wouldn't be as high as you'd expect  since most of the city had already been  evacuated if there were any civilians  then we would have seen them running in  the streets alongside the malian  soldiers but the fact we don't see  anyone implies that the only people left  were involved with the military for that  reason the count only increases by about  15 000 but obviously if aaron keeps  marching then he'll eventually catch up  to all the civilians who tried to run  away  with that said that is the complete kill  count for part 2 of the final season and  like i mentioned in the intro this is  easily more than all the previous  seasons combined if you enjoyed this  video then please drop a like and hit  that sub button so you don't miss new  uploads like this and until the next one  peace out

